{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgLvgaVT2yuLK34cKkekY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking how to handle instance children that can't be removed. I can't remove children of instances at all — they are only overridable via text properties, and instance children cannot be added or removed. So I rebuild the components to have a generic mark area and replace content differently.\n\nThe screen s1 is on canvas. My strategy: build a generic row component with a mark slot that is an instance of a placeholder, then use component properties. I define a text property for ticker/company/price/change and an INSTANCE_SWAP property for the logo. This is a clean design system solution.\n\nI build master components \"Stock Row\" with component properties: ticker (TEXT), company (TEXT), price (TEXT), change (TEXT), Logo (INSTANCE_SWAP), and variant Trend=Gain/Loss for the change color. Figma supports addComponentProperty on the component and setProperties on instances. Adding INSTANCE_SWAP requires preferredValues node ids.\n\nSteps: delete the partial screen 01, rebuild components 9:33/9:44/9:55/9:66 with component properties, rebuild the screens. I create a placeholder \"Mark·","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":51681,"input_tokens":1,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":51681}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6dc355e0-32b3-4413-a395-2651983398f3","uuid":"04ac7785-051f-4296-b127-dfe2fe82eb35","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:27:55.211Z","thinking_duration_ms":15053}
